# Public site bandwidth budget (hard rule)

Operator directive (Phil, 2026-10-30), after Webflow Technical Support
(Marcel) reconciled analoginfo.com usage:

> **We have used an excessive amount of bandwidth creating and testing
> analoginfo.com. Change strategy as a set of new hard rules.**

Support estimates for the reviewed period (not exact byte counts; they
reconciled to about 94% of reported usage; 1 GB = 1,000,000,000 bytes;
timestamps UTC): 43.99 GB total versus 18.27 GB of named assets. The
gap is page delivery. Roughly 10 GB was 404 responses. Staging
`analoginfo-b2base-site.webflow.io` was about 4.3 GB (about 10%).
98% of page traffic and 95% of asset traffic scored as automated.
Likely-human traffic was under 1 GB. Cached Content Delivery Network
(CDN) delivery still counted. Nothing was charged; the site stayed
inside the 50 GB allowance. That is not permission to keep the old
pattern.

A large share carried Analog Informatics User-Agents
(`AnalogInformatics-SiteAudit/1.0`, `AIC-indexnow`,
`AnalogInformatics-Subscriptions/1.0`) plus Python scripting and
Cursor / ChatGPT editor sessions. Support asked AIC to confirm those
are ours and to point tooling at a copy or throttle it.

ChatGPT already shipped production remediation
`bandwidth-20261030-r1` (lean 404, IndexNow explicit URLs, blog
delivery images). Do not replay that release. Do not re-upload those
images. These Cursor rules bind every later chat.

## The rule

> **analoginfo.com and its Webflow staging hostname are production
> bandwidth. They are not a lab. Work from a local copy first. Every
> live request is named, bounded, serialized, and required by the
> current change. Staging counts toward the same Webflow allowance.
> A cached CDN hit still bills. Do not raise limits or split a job
> to evade them. Do not weaken required search, layout, comparison,
> or IndexNow gates to save bytes.**

"A copy of the site" means local HTML, artwork, PDFs, screenshots, and
verified caches on disk. It does **not** mean Webflow staging.

## Hosts that bill

| Host | Role |
| --- | --- |
| `https://analoginfo.com` | Production. Publish here only. |
| `https://analoginfo-b2base-site.webflow.io` | Staging. Same allowance. Do not publish or test here to "save" production. |
| `www.analoginfo.com` | Redirect only. Do not fetch it as a second copy of a page. |

## Offline first

Before any network call:

1. Search existing local HTML, original artwork, uploaded derivatives,
   PDFs, screenshots, release receipts, and hash-verified caches.
2. Reuse a prior receipt when the page, shared layout, and assets did
   not change.
3. Do not recrawl to rediscover facts already saved.

Canonical workflow:
`pam-platform-docs/docs/go-to-market/website-and-ui/TESTING-BANDWIDTH-WORKFLOW-2026-10-28.md`.
Canonical validator (do not invent a second crawler):
`C:/Users/phil/Documents/Codex/2026-10-28/use-work-mode-stay-in-work/work/propagation/validate_search_release.py`
with adjacent `bandwidth_http.py` and `bandwidth_assets.py`. Preserve
`http-cache/`, `asset-cache/`, and `http-transfer-ledger.json`. Do not
copy those clients into a fresh workspace to reset the ledger.

## Live request budget (scripted HTML)

All scripted production HTML requests use `bandwidth_http.py`:

| Limit | Value |
| --- | --- |
| Encoded response-body bytes per run | 12,000,000 |
| Requests per run | 120 |
| Shared UTC-day encoded bytes | 50,000,000 |
| Shared UTC-day requests | 300 |
| Concurrency | One request at a time |
| Spacing | At least one second between requests |

When the budget is exhausted: stop, investigate, and use local
evidence. Never raise the numbers. Never split one job into parallel
processes to reset the counters. Browser traffic and Application
Programming Interface (API) traffic are additional and must be
minimized separately. These client counts are not Webflow's bill.

## Named User-Agent

Never send an empty User-Agent. Every AIC request identifies the
program and a contact:

| Purpose | User-Agent |
| --- | --- |
| Validation | `AnalogInformatics-Validation/3.0 (+https://analoginfo.com/contact)` |
| IndexNow | `AnalogInformatics-IndexNow/2.0 (+https://analoginfo.com/contact)` |

Retired. Do not emit, revive, or "improve":

- `AnalogInformatics-SiteAudit/1.0` (discovery crawler; concurrent;
  guessed paths)
- `AIC-indexnow` (whole-sitemap default)

`AnalogInformatics-Subscriptions/1.0` was seen in Webflow data and
was **not** found in examined AIC code. Ownership and its share of
traffic are unconfirmed. Do not claim all automated traffic is
controlled. Do not invent a Subscriptions crawler to match the name.

Cursor, ChatGPT desktop, Playwright, and Python `urllib` / `requests`
sessions that hit analoginfo.com count. Headless Chrome referred from
our own site counts. A missing User-Agent is forbidden.

## Browser sessions

Visual and functional checks remain mandatory
([`essential-ui-actions-must-be-visible.mdc`](essential-ui-actions-must-be-visible.mdc),
approved comparison layout at 1440 / 390 / 320). Resize the same
loaded tab. Do not open a fresh session per viewport. Do not repeat
screenshots after an unchanged check. Keep graphics, Cascading Style
Sheets (CSS), fonts, and scripts on for visual QA. Do not disable
them to obtain a low transfer count.

ChatGPT 6 desktop Work mode still applies
([`chatgpt-desktop-work-mode.mdc`](chatgpt-desktop-work-mode.mdc)).
Work mode is not a license to crawl production.

## What must stay

Do not drop these to save bandwidth:

- One apex canonical and indexable HTML except `/search`
- Non-empty image alt text and complete ImageObject fields
- JSON-LD / Open Graph that name Analog Informatics Corporation and
  both products
- IndexNow of **explicit changed** production URLs after a real publish
- All-blog pre/post release gate when a blog release is in scope
- 61-question comparison coverage when a comparison page is in scope
- Privacy-preferences launcher on the 404 page

## Forbidden

- Treating analoginfo.com or Webflow staging as a free test target
- Publishing staging, or testing against staging, to avoid production
- Raising run/day limits or splitting jobs to evade them
- Empty User-Agent, or a generic `python-requests` / `curl` default
- Cache-bypass headers, random query strings, or hidden GET fallbacks
- Automatic retry loops
- Replaying `bandwidth-20261030-r1` or re-uploading its images
- Claiming exact monthly savings or a guaranteed billing drop
- Paid plans, Domain Name System (DNS) / proxy changes, or blanket
  search-bot blocks as a bandwidth workaround without a separate
  operator instruction
- Weakening required validation to report a low transfer count

## Required agent behavior

1. Local copy first. Live second. Staging never.
2. Name the User-Agent. Bound the run. Record bytes actually read.
3. After a real production publish, compare the Webflow usage view
   once when available. Do not poll it.
4. Mirror this file to `core-assets/.cursor/rules/` in the same
   change set ([`auto-commit-push.mdc`](auto-commit-push.mdc)).

